@GatewayAddr = http://localhost:5272

### Buffer depth. Run this while the cloud is stopped and watch it climb.
GET {{GatewayAddr}}/buffer

### Inject a reading as if it came from a sensor.
### MessageId is minted by the CALLER on purpose -- that is the whole point.
### Sensor traffic requires a per-device client certificate whose subject matches
### the equipment ID, so this plaintext POST returns 403 by design. To inject with
### the EQ-0 device key, copy device-EQ-0.pfx out of the sensor_tls_data volume and run:
### curl -k --cert-type p12 --cert ./device-EQ-0.pfx: \
###   -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @reading.json \
###   https://localhost:5273/api/local/telemetry
### (scripts/e2e.sh post_edge_reading shows the same exchange inside Compose.)
POST {{GatewayAddr}}/api/local/telemetry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messageId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "equipmentId": "EQ-99",
  "sequenceNumber": 1,
  "occurredAt": "2026-08-21T12:00:00Z",
  "engineTemperature": 245.0,
  "oilPressure": 42.5
}

### Send the request above twice. Both return 202, one row is buffered.
### The unique index on MessageId collapses the retry.
